# Preserve exact bytes for hash-verified scientific outputs.
#
# Several run manifests record SHA-256 of Windows CRLF bytes, and the API
# verifies files byte-for-byte (a mismatch returns 503). Git's default
# end-of-line conversion would rewrite these files on checkout and break
# those checks. Marking them "-text" keeps the working-tree bytes unchanged
# on every platform.

* text=auto

# Never convert line endings in data files that are hash-verified
*.csv   -text
*.tsv   -text
*.txt   -text
*.json  -text
*.jsonl -text
*.rds   binary
*.RData binary

# Binary assets
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.gz    binary
*.gctx  binary
*.h5    binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
